  "label": "students or history class participants",
  "description": "The meme targets individuals who have experienced or are familiar with the emotional impact of learning about the Holocaust in a history class, particularly students who may feel overwhelmed or distressed during such discussions. The visual of two people covering their mouths in distress, paired with the text 'when your history teacher starts talking about the holocaust,' is designed to resonate with students who have encountered this topic in school, implying a shared, exaggerated emotional reaction. The target community is likely young adults or teenagers who have been exposed to Holocaust education in a formal educational setting.",
